<title>USA: TABLE - Rogers Corp Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Rogers Corp Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>ROGERS, Conn. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Statements of Income</p>
<p>				     Quarters Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					Jun 29, Jun 30, Jun 29, Jun 30,</p>
<p>					   1997    1996    1997    1996</p>
<p>(In Thousands, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p> Net Sales			  $45,788 $35,424 $90,128 $70,362</p>
<p>Costs and Expenses:</p>
<p>  Cost of Sales		    32,183  24,145  63,449  47,562</p>
<p>  Selling and Administrative    6,179   5,362  11,789  10,775</p>
<p>  Research and Development	2,516   2,303   4,967   4,721</p>
<p>Total Costs and Expenses</p>
<p>(Including Depreciation</p>
<p>of:  1997 - $3,902; 1996 -</p>
<p>  $3,217)(A)			 40,878  31,810  80,205  63,058</p>
<p> Operating Income		   4,910   3,614   9,923   7,304</p>
<p>Other Income less Other</p>
<p>   Charges				520     865     934   1,380</p>
<p>  Interest Income, Net		194     118     301     177</p>
<p>  Income Before Income Taxes    5,624   4,597  11,158   8,861</p>
<p> Income Taxes			 1,519   1,057   3,013   2,038</p>
<p> Net Income			   4,105   3,540   8,145   6,823</p>
<p>Net Income Per Share:(B)</p>
<p>  Primary				 .53    0.47    1.05    0.91</p>
<p>  Fully Diluted			 .52    0.47    1.04    0.90</p>
<p>Shares Used in Computing:</p>
<p>  Primary			     7,801   7,570   7,770   7,527</p>
<p>  Fully Diluted		     7,862   7,570   7,854   7,548</p>
<p>NOTE(A):  For the six month periods.</p>
<p>NOTE(B):  Basic Net Income Per Share as defined in Statement of Financial Accounting Standards No. 128 was $0.55 and $0.49 for the second quarters of 1997 and 1996, respectively, and $1.09 and $0.95 for the comparable six month periods ending June 29, 1997 and June 30, 1996, respectively.</p>
<p>These statements are subject to year-end audit.</p>
